# CLAUDE.md

{{description}}

This is a [SwissKitJ](https://github.com/MuskStark/SwissKitJ) plugin — `{{plugin-id}}`
(`{{Name}}`, base package `{{base-package}}`). It builds independently as a standalone Maven
project and is dropped into the host's `.swisskit/plugin/` directory as a fat JAR at runtime.

## Build & Run

```bash
# Preview inside a SwissKitJ-like shell (fast iteration loop)
mvn -Pdev javafx:run

# Production fat JAR (SPI + dependencies merged via maven-shade-plugin)
mvn package
# Output: target/{{plugin-name}}-1.0.0.jar
# Deploy: copy the JAR into the host's <user.dir>/.swisskit/plugin/ directory (hot-reload supported)
```

`swisskit.api.version` in `pom.xml` currently pins `SwissKitJ-Api` to `{{swisskit-api-version}}`
— bump it only when targeting a newer host release, and re-run `bash validate.sh .` after.

## Hard constraints

These are enforced mechanically by `validate.sh` (see below) or reviewed semantically by the
`swisskitj-plugin-reviewer` agent. Do not regress them:

- **SPI registration**: entry class FQN, one line, at
  `src/main/resources/META-INF/services/fan.summer.zhiflow.api.SwissKitJPlugin`; must match an
  actual `.java` file on this exact path.
- **`SwissKitJ-Api` dependency scope is `provided`** — the host supplies it at runtime; do
  not shade it into the fat JAR.
- **Shade plugin must configure `ServicesResourceTransformer`** — without it, SPI files
  from dependencies get silently overwritten in the fat JAR and the plugin fails to load.
- **Use `.sk-*` style classes / `-sk-*` CSS tokens, never `.glass-*`** — the old
  glassmorphism utility classes were renamed away in host v3.2.0.
- **Layout pitfalls (JavaFX)** — one line each, see `standards/pitfalls.md` /
  `standards/ui.md` in the plugin-kit for the full detail:
  - Never `setPrefWidth(Double.MAX_VALUE)` — use `setMaxWidth(Double.MAX_VALUE)` +
    `HBox/VBox.setHgrow/Vgrow(node, Priority.ALWAYS)` instead.
  - Never bind `maxWidthProperty()` to the node's own `widthProperty()` — it's circular and
    collapses layout to the min size.
  - When toggling pages inside a `StackPane`, toggle both `setVisible` and `setManaged`.
- **i18n bundle registration**: `createView()` (or `init(PluginHost)`) must register the
  bundle before any UI is built — `I18n.registerPluginBundle("i18n.messages",
  getClass().getClassLoader())` or `host.i18n().registerBundle("i18n.messages")`. Both
  `i18n/messages.properties` and `i18n/messages_zh.properties` must exist with identical
  key sets, prefixed `plugin.{{slug}}.`.
- **`getId()` is reverse-domain** (at least two dot-separated segments), returned verbatim,
  e.g. `{{plugin-id}}`.
- **`DevLauncher.java` has zero JavaFX references** — no `import javafx...` and no
  fully-qualified `javafx.*` usage anywhere in the file. All JavaFX (including
  `Platform.startup`) lives in a separate `DevApp.java` in the same package; `DevLauncher`
  only calls `DevApp.main(args)`. Any `javafx` reference in `DevLauncher.java` breaks `mvn
  javafx:run -Pdev` with a module-system error and fails `validate.sh` M11.

## Standing instruction

**After ANY change, run `bash validate.sh .`** from this repo's root and fix every `FAIL`
line before moving on. **Before packaging** (`mvn package`) or opening a PR, review the
project with the `swisskitj-plugin-reviewer` agent and resolve every reported violation —
it checks the semantic rules (`AiTool` JSON contract, background work via `host.tasks()`,
`Themes.applyTo(scene)` on self-built windows, H2 path conventions, `createView()` caching
discipline, `-sk-*` token usage) that `validate.sh` cannot check mechanically.
